Good afternoon,

We are instructed to notify a water intrusion loss on the Northfield Senior Living development in Madison. Our reference is KRP/CAR/2025/6612.

I am travelling and do not have the policy schedule with me - the binder is with our Tulsa office - so please locate on our reference and the project. The first named insured is Sundale Property Group, LLC of Tulsa and the general contractor is Halcyon Builders, LLC of Madison.

Broker reference: KRP/CAR/2025/6612
Project name: Northfield Senior Living
Contract number: AIA-A133-2024-NSL
Insured name: Sundale Property Group, LLC
General contractor: Halcyon Builders, LLC
Date of loss: 18 October 2025
Loss location: 1725 Northfield Commons Drive, Madison, WI 53704
Estimated loss: USD 915,000

A frontal system put 2.81 inches of rain through Dane County over the weekend
with gusts to 44 mph. Two unflashed mechanical curbs and the elevator overrun
took water directly, and the wind tore most of the temporary poly off the north
elevation at Levels 3 and 4.

Nobody was on site over the weekend so it ran until Monday morning. Servpro were
in by 09:00 Monday and there are daily moisture logs from first attendance.

There is schedule float, but the drying and controlled demolition will cost two
to three weeks on the Building A critical path. If that becomes a delay we will
revert on the soft costs section - the owner entities are the named insureds for it.

Attached:

  * the completed loss notice
  * drying and moisture report
  * reinstatement schedule

Please confirm a claim reference and an adjuster. Owen at Halcyon can meet
anyone on site with 24 hours' notice.

